################################################################################
## Exploratory Specific Sleep Complaints Longitudinal Network Temperature Analysis
##
## Purpose:
##   Evaluate longitudinal network temperature trajectories and temperature divergence 
##   (Delta-Delta-T) across five specific baseline sleep complaint phenotypes:
##     1. No complaint (0 items positive)
##     2. Difficulty falling asleep only (Q44 positive only)
##     3. Early awakening only (Q64 positive only)
##     4. Superficial sleep only (Q66 positive only)
##     5. Multiple complaints (>=2 items positive)
##
## Features:
##   - Item binarization (score >= 1 as positive).
##   - Group-specific constrained Ising models (equal omega and tau across waves).
##   - Stratified participant-level ID bootstrap for 95% CIs.
##   - Benjamini-Hochberg (BH) False Discovery Rate (FDR) adjustment across the four 
##     focal comparisons within each symptom domain at T5.
##   - Automated generation of publication-ready summary text and tables for Results 3.8.
################################################################################

